## 2. Problem, outcome and scope

Packaged MCP smoke can falsely accept an error/failing process. Legacy existing-tag recovery omits the current-main ancestry guard. PowerShell installer probes can accept native nonzero exits before replacement. The Rust-only gate rejects all docs Python, contrary to the selected bounded documentation policy. The approved COD-108 scope reduces repeated heavy CI only for positively verified metadata-only release PRs. COD-110 adds premerge candidate readiness and moves final deterministic crate verification ahead of public mutation; ordinary repository policy already runs in PR/main CI and is not newly invented by COD-110.

Outcome: restore the three existing failure barriers; permit the selected docs-only helper boundary; reduce heavy release-PR CI only for positively verified metadata-only changes; deliver all accepted children as a real ordered PR stack, integrate serially, and release the complete authorized source and artifact set. Proposed COD-110 additionally catches deterministic candidate defects before release-PR merge and crate defects before public mutation, while retaining the final exact-release barrier.

**Existing approved scope:** COD-105/106/56/107/108, stack qualification staging, PR158 selected subset, exact-source release evidence and delivery. **Proposed amendment:** append COD-110, its bounded preflight/verification ordering and necessary exact stack-base qualification extension; include the selected already-merged COD-54 subset in the final reconciled release contents.

**Excluded:** reopening COD-104/COD-99; removing admin bypass; product/dependency license changes or inferred relicensing of helpers/evidence; new supported platforms; a two-heavy-run alternative; new publication permissions/privileged PR triggers; PR-artifact promotion; weakening exact-SHA CI/provenance/security gates; two-binary rollback redesign; unrequested helper restoration; automatic COD-53/COD-54/platform milestone/parent aggregate closure; conda distribution selection; unknown later main delta without reconciliation and approval.

Only current approved native targets **macOS ARM64 and Windows x86_64** apply. Stale four-target skill/wiki wording must be reconciled as procedure, not used to expand platform support.

## 3. Requirements

The `C103-` IDs below belong only to this combined delivery specification. They do not replace child identities or platform R05/A09.

### C103-R01 — Successful packaged MCP smoke (COD-105)

A packaged graph MCP smoke passes only when the child completes successfully and valid JSON-RPC responses for the expected initialize and tools/list request IDs demonstrate successful initialization and an actual tools entry named `graph_search`.

Nonzero status, response errors, missing required response, malformed protocol data and a missing tool fail artifact acceptance. Error-message substrings cannot establish success. Report useful status/protocol diagnostics. This restores the current release contract; it does not define a new product protocol.

### C103-R02 — Main-history source in legacy recovery (COD-106)

Every publication source, including existing-tag native-assets-only recovery, must remain in current main history. Sources identical to or ancestors of current main are valid; removed/diverged sources are not. Establish ancestry before authorizing recovery and recheck before the legacy asset mutation.

Preserve strict tags, exact-source successful main-push CI, complete artifact/provenance checks, dry-run, historical tags without release-PR linkage, native-assets-only legacy scope and original source identity. Do not require current main-tip equality or add crate publication to this recovery mode.

### External requirement — CBG-PLAT-01/S05 R05/A09 (COD-56)

Implement and qualify the existing platform requirement **in place**. Every native probe's nonzero exit must fail before either destination binary is replaced; both binaries must pass existing checksum/probe validation first. Reuse all A09 success/failure/DryRun/destination-preservation cases and both approved PowerShell shell families on the approved Windows desktop scope. Do not restate or renumber the platform acceptance contract here.

### C103-R03 — Bounded docs helpers (COD-107)

The approved path boundary is `docs/` only. Retain the revision0.2 combined-approved constraints:

- Allowed content is documentation, evidence, qualification, audit or reproduction support, not product runtime/build/install implementation.
- Helpers may be explicitly invoked by developers as **optional Python 3 standard-library-only local commands**. This slice adds no Python dependency, package/tool manifest, setup or invocation in CI, Release, product build, runtime or installation. Existing workflow Python prohibitions remain.
- Helpers are absent from shipped native archives and publishable `.crate` payloads. Ordinary Git/tag source snapshots may contain documentation; this is not an executable distribution dependency.
- Existing prohibited Python surfaces outside docs and prohibited root tooling remain rejected. No docs-path allowance exempts other repository/security/workflow checks.
- No automatic extraction/restoration of COD-99 archived helpers. Preserve archive bytes, reconstruction notes and historical decisions.

These constraints are settled by the exact revision0.2 combined approval; COD-110 does not reopen them.

### C103-R04 — Positively verified metadata-only PR mode (COD-108)

Only a current trusted repository-owned release PR with a positively verified **actual base/head semantic diff** may use lightweight CI. Branch, label, title or small diff alone is insufficient. Every ordinary PR and **every push to main**, including a release-PR merge, keeps full CI and exact-source native artifacts.

Retain the revision0.2 approved exact semantic allowlist:

- `.release-please-manifest.json`: root `.` release version only.
- `Cargo.toml`: root package.version only.
- `crates/k-wiki/Cargo.toml`: package.version and local codebase-graph dependency.version only.
- `crates/xtask/Cargo.toml`: package.version only.
- `Cargo.lock`: only corresponding codebase-graph/k-wiki/xtask workspace package-version identities; no external package resolution, checksum, source or dependency-edge changes.
- `CHANGELOG.md`: consistent new version-specific release section; no rewriting historical sections.

All fields/versions must agree. All other changes run full CI. Real generated release PR #165 includes xtask and workspace-lock version bumps; a blanket lockfile exclusion would reject the intended positive case.

Trust must verify current same-repository head/base and expected configured release identity; actual semantic diff proof is still mandatory. Do not presume a bot username without verifying the configured proposal-token identity.

Retain the approved mandatory lightweight checks: positive classifier, repository/workflow policy, metadata/version/changelog consistency, formatting, and the existing advisory scan. Heavy native/test/artifact/package/lint jobs may be skipped only for this positively established mode. Report skips as skips. Code, workflows, dependencies, build, packaging, features, installers or uncertain acquisition/classification use **full CI**; no silent lightweight fallback.

### C103-R05 — Stable, fresh required result and stack qualification

Keep exactly one stable `required` result for each qualified PR. The result must be based on the selected valid mode and that mode's mandatory successful checks. Failed/cancelled checks, missing/invalid classification or unexpected job states cannot make it green. Intentional heavy skips are accepted only with positive fresh lightweight evidence.

A changed head or base must invalidate previous classification/qualification. Preserve strict-freshness enforcement and the intentionally retained admin bypass; do not claim a bypass-capable actor provides server enforcement.

Approved true-PR-stack order remains **COD-105 → COD-106 → COD-56 → COD-107 → COD-108**. Proposed revision0.3 appends **→ COD-110** only after separate exact-scope approval. The new true child requires a narrow extension for initial base `cod103-stack/cod-108` alongside the approved literal bases; the exact trigger/typed-policy/tests and prerequisite ownership must be settled in design/delivery/Scryer before dependent staging. No wildcard or main-only push/release expansion is implied. The stack CI/staging prerequisite may be delivered as part of first-PR staging under the approved combined scope. The technical proposal must specify how non-main-base stack PRs gain valid qualification under currently main-only PR triggers. It may not silently discard stacking, introduce an unapproved privileged trigger or accept missing/greenless required checks. Any approved staging exception to default merge-before-next-implementation must be explicit in the fixed queue record. The [delivery index](delivery.md#first-child-staging-clarification-pr-01) distinguishes COD-105 staging-only handoff from full qualification: its own applicable local/artifact/full-main-base-PR checks and independent final review/fix verification permit opening COD-106 solely to obtain the deferred first-child non-main-base full-CI proof. Production obtains it, Evidence Verifier records it against C103-A05, and Engineer links both existing ledgers. Missing/failed/stale proof blocks full COD-105 qualification, COD-106 handoff to COD-56, every actual main integration, Done and release. Later per-PR retarget proof remains due at its actual stage, not as a prerequisite to opening its own PR. No evidence is waived or presumed passed.

Each child starts with a fresh implementation session; do not reuse an implementer across issue boundaries. Keep one active implementation issue and one writer per file.

Integrate actual main merges serially. Require successful full main CI for each actual merge before the next integration step. Shared ownership and implementation details remain in Scryer.

### C103-R06 — Complete authorized release and retained ownership

Under existing rev0.2 approval, release only the complete five-item queue and its authorized contents. Under this separately approved amendment, release only when **all six selected children, including COD-110**, satisfy their exact acceptance/review/verification gates, the approved full unreleased delta is reconciled, and the exact release candidate passes applicable gates. Include PR158's approved and COD-54's selected already-merged subsets only where still unreleased; selection is not COD-53/COD-54 or platform closure and does not approve unknown later changes. Do not silently expand or partially release either queue.

Publication remains bound to the release merge's own successful main-push CI, exact native artifacts, protected production confirmations, complete provenance/validation and existing recovery/finalization rules. Keep the current release process and supported targets. Final candidate review and independent publication verification are required before reporting release complete.

No partial queue release or silent qualification deferral. Parent COD-103, COD-51, COD-61 and platform milestone aggregate closure stay with their existing maintainer/user owner; a release or completed child does not automatically close them.

### C103-R07 — Shared secret-free release-candidate preflight (COD-110, proposed)

Every qualifying PR must pass the one always-mandatory common repository-policy lane retained from COD-108, including lightweight mode. Preserve existing policy checks; do not duplicate them in a competing lane or leave them only in a heavy job that lightweight mode skips.

Before a release PR may merge, required preflight must validate its **actual tested checkout identity and proposed version**, using the same core metadata validation as the final selected main source. Require agreement of root/wiki/xtask package versions, the local codebase-graph dependency version, release manifest, permitted workspace lock identities and one consistent nonempty matching changelog section. Reuse R04's exact allowed semantic contract; external dependency changes are not metadata-only. A failed, unavailable, missing or stale mandatory preflight cannot produce successful `required`. Changed tested head/base invalidates prior readiness under R05. A valid candidate creates no tag/release and grants neither lightweight eligibility nor publication authorization.

Ordinary non-release PRs retain all existing repository-policy/release-sync checks and full CI, but gain no obligation to invent a future version, tag or release note, or satisfy a release-PR-only candidate transition. Shared core validation must preserve these caller-specific obligations rather than applying candidate-only checks to every ordinary PR. For a release PR and the final selected release source, require the one nonempty section matching the actual proposed/selected version; lightweight admission additionally retains R04's new-version-section-only/no-historical-rewrite rule. PR execution remains secret-free: no protected `cargo` environment, publishing credentials, hardcoded owner confirmations, privileged PR trigger or widened deployment rules. Current owner-controlled production authorization is checked again at publication, not inferred from a green PR.

### C103-R08 — Verify the exact crate before public mutation (COD-110, proposed)

For automatic/CI-run modes that publish the crate, final dry-run package verification and the existing exact compressed-size limit must succeed for the **same selected immutable release source** before creating its tag, creating/publishing a public GitHub Release or uploading native assets. Reuse that successful source/version-bound verification result through the guarded publication sequence; no second divergent validator or substitute source/run may authorize mutation. This is not an obligation to upload the exact preflight archive bytes: ordinary Cargo publication may repackage the unchanged selected source/version. Exact build-once/promote archive identity remains mandatory for native artifacts. Do not introduce a new registry client merely to upload a supplied `.crate`. A dry-run/size failure permits none of those mutations. Existing-tag recovery remains native-assets-only; this does not add crate publication to that mode.

After verification, preserve native publication before actual crate **upload**, including the existing draft → asset upload → complete asset readback/byte verification → publication ordering. Already-published immutable releases remain verification-only where recovery requires; never repair them by forbidden uploads. Preserve registry-aware exact-version retries, partial-outcome reconciliation and finalization only after native assets and crate succeed. If the exact version is already authoritatively visible, retain upload success/no-upload recovery; still perform nonmutating exact-source package verification and size validation before any pending public mutation. Use a verification path compatible with that already-published state rather than failing solely because the registry version exists. Registry visibility does not replace source/package verification, and package verification does not authorize a duplicate upload.

Premerge success cannot replace final validation of the actual release-merge SHA and its own successful full main CI/run/attempt, current main ancestry, selected metadata/tag/version, complete exact-run two-target artifacts/checksums/provenance, current owner-controlled authorization and nonconflicting tag/registry state. Build once on main and promote those artifacts, never PR artifacts. Changed immutable source requires fresh exact-source qualification, not reuse of an old candidate's evidence.

## 4. Failure, recovery, permissions and privacy

- Smoke/probe failure stops acceptance or replacement, preserves existing installed bytes where A09 requires, and retains useful failure evidence. A source read, child status or malformed-response failure cannot become a pass.
- Failed/unavailable ancestry comparison blocks publication. If main changes invalidate source before mutation, stop; retry only after re-establishing valid source. Never move a tag or clear pending labels to bypass identity or publication gates.
- Diff/API ambiguity, failed/partial acquisition, unsupported file/field, rename/delete or stale base/head cannot select lightweight mode. Use full CI; if the mode result itself is invalid/missing, `required` must not succeed. Retries must use current identity/diff, not stale success.
- Candidate-preflight failure blocks release-PR merge readiness without creating public state. Final crate verification failure blocks tag creation, public release creation/publication and native upload; preserve diagnostics and the selected source. Corrected source needs its own qualification; unchanged verified candidates may resume only under the existing governed exact-target recovery rules. External authorization/service failures can still stop publication after PR success.
- No conda distribution is selected. Keep the existing optional policy; if explicitly selected later, settle nonsecret premerge source checks and the future archive-digest stage before changing that path. Never silently disable a required check because an environment toggle is unavailable.
- Cancellation/failed jobs cannot authorize merge or publication. Preserve failed attempts and exact rerun identity. Partial external publication uses the existing exact-target recovery process; no substitute SHA/run, mixed artifact source or premature finalization.
- No automatic account/token/settings changes or new secret permissions. Use existing read-only PR qualification posture. Do not paste tokens into chat or commit credentials/private runtime state in evidence. Retain only relevant source/run IDs, hashes, OS/shell versions and necessary redacted diagnostics.
- The authenticated admin always-bypass identity is not the required enforceable merge path. An **authorized non-bypass merge actor** remains a capability gate before integration/release; preserve the user's bypass choice and do not replace server enforcement with a weaker local-only merge check.
- **Actual Windows 11 desktop PowerShell 5.1 and supported 7 execution** remains a capability/evidence gate for COD-56 A09. Windows Server CI, macOS PowerShell, configured jobs and source traces are not substitutes. If unavailable, keep acceptance/release pending; do not reduce the approved support contract.
- **Qualification route, user2026-10-30:** “the windows 11 tests will be done on windows machine once the PRs are pushed” ([COD-103 decision](https://linear.app/codebasegraph/issue/COD-103#comment-1ce18dd1-e446-468d-b491-3b5b7ecb0edf), [COD-56 record](https://linear.app/codebasegraph/issue/COD-56#comment-62b8347d-ebc5-41e7-b639-5fbe7dac415d)). Push the reviewed PR first; the user then runs the unchanged A09 matrix on actual Windows11 x86_64 desktop under built-in PowerShell5.1 and supported7, followed by independent evidence acceptance. No local runner provisioning is required before push. This is sequencing only, not a pass, waiver, endpoint or predecessor/staging/one-active-issue gate change; COD-56 acceptance and release remain pending actual accepted evidence. The authorized non-bypass merger remains a separate gate.

